{
  slug: 'performance-profiling-your-app-with-procexp',
  title: 'Performance profiling your app with Procexp',
  date: '2025-02-20',
  sourceUrl: 'https://www.ryanjohnson.website/8221/',
  capturedAt: '2026-07-22',
  excerpt: "If you want to ever see how much CPU or GPU a particular process is using over time, use Sysinternals Process Explorer (procexp) and find the process, open up its properties, and have a look at the Performance Graph and GPU Graph. This is a feature I didn't know existed in Procexp, but I have [&hellip;]",
  contentHtml: '\n<p>If you want to ever see how much CPU or GPU a particular process is using over time, use Sysinternals Process Explorer (procexp) and find the process, open up its properties, and have a look at the Performance Graph and GPU Graph. This is a feature I didn&#8217;t know existed in Procexp, but I have used Procexp in the past to kill tasks that were difficult to identify (chrome.exe, anyone?). Certain apps like Chrome and most browsers create dozens of copies of the same executable name, for their tabs.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img data-dominant-color="d0d2d8" data-has-transparency="false" style="--dominant-color: #d0d2d8;" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="967" height="912" sizes="auto, (max-width: 967px) 100vw, 967px" src="https://www.ryanjohnson.website/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/image-8-png.avif" alt="" class="wp-image-8224 not-transparent" srcset="https://www.ryanjohnson.website/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/image-8-png.avif 967w, https://www.ryanjohnson.website/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/image-8-500x472.avif 500w, https://www.ryanjohnson.website/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/image-8-768x724.avif 768w" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>If you ever have a window that is misbehaving and you need to identify its process, use the cross-hairs to snipe it on screen. Just drag and drop the cross-hairs onto the app.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img data-dominant-color="c2c4cb" data-has-transparency="false" style="--dominant-color: #c2c4cb;" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1024" height="654" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" src="https://www.ryanjohnson.website/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/image-9-1024x654.avif" alt="" class="wp-image-8225 not-transparent" srcset="https://www.ryanjohnson.website/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/image-9-1024x654.avif 1024w, https://www.ryanjohnson.website/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/image-9-500x319.avif 500w, https://www.ryanjohnson.website/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/image-9-768x490.avif 768w, https://www.ryanjohnson.website/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/image-9-png.avif 1292w" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Dragging the cross-hair onto a window will outline the window, and then locate its executable in the process call tree.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img data-dominant-color="c3c2c2" data-has-transparency="false" style="--dominant-color: #c3c2c2;" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="746" height="741" sizes="auto, (max-width: 746px) 100vw, 746px" src="https://www.ryanjohnson.website/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/image-10-png.avif" alt="" class="wp-image-8226 not-transparent" srcset="https://www.ryanjohnson.website/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/image-10-png.avif 746w, https://www.ryanjohnson.website/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/image-10-500x497.avif 500w, https://www.ryanjohnson.website/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/image-10-150x150.avif 150w" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img data-dominant-color="d7d7e4" data-has-transparency="false" style="--dominant-color: #d7d7e4;" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="786" height="898" sizes="auto, (max-width: 786px) 100vw, 786px" src="https://www.ryanjohnson.website/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/image-11-png.avif" alt="" class="wp-image-8227 not-transparent" srcset="https://www.ryanjohnson.website/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/image-11-png.avif 786w, https://www.ryanjohnson.website/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/image-11-438x500.avif 438w, https://www.ryanjohnson.website/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/image-11-768x877.avif 768w" /></figure>\n',
  wordpressId: 8221,
}
